    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the suite, and it passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule in the owner-creation endpoint (`POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).\n\n**Changes to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a capacity guard in `addOwner`, right after field normalization and before saving:\n   ```java\n   if (cityIsAtCapacity(owner.getCity())) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. Added the `cityIsAtCapacity` helper, which counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed \u2014 consistent with the existing `nextCustomerCode` city logic) and returns `true` when the count is 50 or more.\n\nWhen the owner's city already contains 50+ owners, creation is rejected with **409 Conflict**. The acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` \u2014 fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to be rejected) and the full suite pass.",
